  "result": "Fixed: a subcommand now picks up its own section of the parent's `default_map`, so your example prints `changed`.\n\nIn `Context.__init__` (`src/click/core.py`), a child context was inheriting the parent's entire `default_map`. It now takes `parent.default_map.get(info_name)`, so `default_map={'foo': {'name': 'changed'}}` reaches `foo` as `{'name': 'changed'}`.\n\nI added `test_group_subcommand_default_map` to `tests/test_commands.py`. It checks that `foo` prints `changed` with the default map and `normal` without it. I didn't run the new test against the old code to confirm it fails there.\n\n`python -m pytest tests/test_commands.py tests/test_defaults.py -q` gives 145 passed.",
